{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"scarlet-wroth-ratfish","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Problem\nGerrit change 2973 (cohort 01 comment condensation) merged as `4f12815e9a0b0cee5ded72d73e22256115e10c87`, carrying the receipted revision `86eead289c546d98f2264986d7e4e17d086e050e`. A later author-side candidate, `e393e9a34b1659fa22be712375f5d5889ad14c0e`, applied a documentation-policy pass over the same 124 allowlisted blocks and earned its own four-part independent non-author receipt, but was never pushed and is now unrecoverable — absent from the local object database, every reflog, Gerrit's `rebar.git`, and the MCP gate workspace.\n\nThe merged tree therefore contains the condensation but not the policy pass. The pass covered banned punctuation, banned diction, contractions, lowercase sentence starts, and clause-joining colons, as recorded in the final author-validation comment on `unable-wingless-bustard`. None of this is machine-enforced, which is why CI reported `Verified +1` on `86eead28`.\n\n## Approach\nRe-derive the pass against the merged content rather than trying to recover the lost commit. The inputs that made it reproducible all survive: `docs/documentation-policy.md` states the rules, and the receipts on `unable-wingless-bustard` enumerate the 124 stable IDs across the 20 paths.\n\n1. Resolve the 124 allowlisted stable IDs against the merged tree.\n2. Scan those targets only for the five violation classes named above.\n3. Correct violations without touching executable AST, runtime strings, directives, or protected prose, and without lengthening any target relative to its immutable base.\n4. Regenerate `docs/env-vars.md` and `docs/mcp-reference.md` if any statically generated source-location citation shifts.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The 124 allowlisted stable IDs from the cohort receipts resolve one-for-one against the merged tree, and any that do not are listed with the reason.\n- [ ] A target-only scan of those blocks reports zero banned punctuation, zero banned diction, zero contractions, zero lowercase sentence starts, and zero clause-joining colons.\n- [ ] No executable AST, runtime string, directive, or protected prose region is modified.\n- [ ] Every corrected block remains no longer than its counterpart in the immutable base `2697be85ccc223c245815bc6ad818ebee2915c70`.\n- [ ] Generated artifacts `docs/env-vars.md` and `docs/mcp-reference.md` are regenerated if affected, and `make lint` reports no drift.\n- [ ] The change lands through Gerrit with `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`.","id":"995a-881d-b2dd-40be","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Re-derive lost documentation-policy pass over cohort 01 condensed comments"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1789664887217781775,"uuid":"c8811681-fe8f-4bd7-83ed-3ad01733c760"}